# Stub-run fixtures. Empty placeholders that exist so
# `-profile stub -stub-run` can resolve its reference and input paths;
# they hold no data.
#
# Without these three lines the fixtures cannot be committed at all:
# stub.fa matches the *.fa reference rule, stub.fa.fai matches *.fai, and
# stub.bam matches the *.bam patient-data guard. git add reports them as
# ignored and stages nothing, which is why the fixtures have existed in
# working trees but never in the repository, and why the stub-run workflow
# has never had them.
#
# Named individually rather than un-ignoring tests/refs/, so the
# patient-data guards stay in force everywhere else in the tree.
!tests/refs/stub.fa
!tests/refs/stub.fa.fai
!tests/refs/stub.bam

# Run artifacts
report_v7_*/
report_v7_*.zip
